The Box Model
------------
->Every single element in the browser is a box and we can control different properties of 
  each box.

┌─────────────────────────────┐
│          BORDER             │ ← The line around the box
│  ┌────────────────────────┐ │
│  │        PADDING         │ │
│  │   ┌──────────────────┐ │ │
│  │   │     CONTENT      │ │ │
│  │   └──────────────────┘ │ │
│  └────────────────────────┘ │
└─────────────────────────────┘

Why Do We Use Borders?
---------------------
Borders help you:

• Highlight elements
• Create outlines or boxes
• Make buttons, cards, sections
• Separate content visually
• Debug layout (very useful!)

--------------------------------------------
⭐ BORDER PROPERTIES
--------------------------------------------

1️⃣ BORDER-WIDTH  
Defines how thick the border is.

• Common values:
  - thin
  - medium
  - thick

• Using units:
  border-width: 1px;
  border-width: 5px;
  border-width: 0.2rem;

• Each side can be set separately:
  border-top-width: 3px;
  border-right-width: 2px;
  border-bottom-width: 5px;
  border-left-width: 1px;


2️⃣ BORDER-STYLE (MOST IMPORTANT)  
The border will NOT appear unless a style is set.

• Common styles:
  - solid → continuous line
  - dashed → dashes
  - dotted → dots
  - double → two lines
  - groove → 3D effect
  - ridge → opposite of groove
  - inset → looks pressed in
  - outset → looks pushed out
  - none → no border
  - hidden → similar to none

• Example:
  border-style: dashed;


3️⃣ BORDER-COLOR  
Sets the color of the border.

• Examples:
  border-color: red;
  border-color: #3498db;
  border-color: rgb(20, 200, 40);

• Set different colors for each side:
  border-top-color: red;
  border-right-color: green;
  border-bottom-color: blue;
  border-left-color: yellow;

Border Shorthand Property (All-in-One)
--------------------------------------
border: <border-width> <border-style> <border-color>;

Example:
border: 2px solid blue;

Example
-------
Border for Each Side
---------------------
You can target any side individually:

border-top: 4px solid red;
border-right: 3px dotted green;
border-bottom: 5px double blue;
border-left: 2px dashed purple;

Important Notes
================
-> Border shows only if border-style is set.
-> Border adds to the element’s size.
-> For example, if width = 200px and border = 5px, actual width = 210px.

border: shorthand ALWAYS applies to ALL 4 sides.
===============================================
Example:
   border: 2px solid red;


-->This puts a 2px solid red border on:

top
right
bottom
left

So YES — when you use the shorthand border: it never applies to just one side.

Summary (Easy to Remember)

Property         Applies To
--------------------------------
border:          ALL 4 sides
border-top:      Only top
border-right:    Only right
border-bottom:   Only bottom
border-left:     Only left
